{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The wrong export page counts came from `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py`. It used integer floor division (`total // per_page`), so any remainder rows did not add a page—for example, 101 rows at 10 per page was reported as 10 pages instead of 11.\n\nThat value feeds `page_summary` in `repo/rows.py`, which is what exports use for the `\"pages\"` field and `last_page_start`.\n\nThe fix counts a partial last page with standard ceiling division: `(total + per_page - 1) // per_page`, and returns `0` when `total <= 0`. `old_page_count` still delegates to `num_pages`, so the legacy v1 path gets the same behavior.\n\nAll tests in `tests/visible/test_paging.py` pass."}]},"session_id":"66b74359-884b-4ba1-8fc2-9793fb54c6e3"}
